{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496425-shopping-mall-totem","id":1496425,"title":"Shopping Mall Totem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-07T17:44:09-08:00","id":1496425,"title":"Shopping Mall Totem","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I would like some aid on building a totem.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is the spirit of the oldest and one of the largest malls (about 99 000 m\u00b2 or 1 065 628 ft\u00b2 in size, and 25% additional for parking lots) in the city.<br /> <br /> The mall is inside the city not the outskirts, the adjacent high income neighborhoods grew around the mall as part of the effect of its construction.<br /> <br /> The place has 4 small casinos insides, a large toy stores, 3 food quarters, 2 pharmacies, a couple of book stores, a large hypermarket, a hotel, an internal park, a small vet office, an office building, 12 bank branches, plus an assortment of high end clothing, beauty and accessories stores (not the most expensive ones but high end), a cinema and minor amenities. The mall does not have everything that the people of the area need (there are other businesses outside of it, mostly specialist stores or restaurants), but it tries to have it all.<br /> <br /> It is not open 24x7 but close to it.<br /> <br /> This is a generational pack, that has been working with this spirit for a while. Iron Masters all of them. They either work at the mall administration or in one of its stores, and I envision them living in the surrounding neighborhoods.<br /> <br /> The pack is amenable to having other creatures, but it would be mainly mortals with minor templates or perhaps mages, everything is too hidden or will predate upon the mall clients.<br /> <br /> The pack claims the mall itself as territory but also the adjacent neighborhoods (not sure how big to make the area, the focus of the pack is the mall itself but it is a good policy to protect the annex area and of course, that is where they live).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am looking for aid in the stats of the Totem (about 21 points): <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Name</b>. The name of the mall itself.</li> <li><b>Rank</b>. A standard Rank 3 creature.</li> <li><b>Appereance</b>. It should look as the mortal building itself which would give it an absurd size (and therefore health) but would have to have Speed 0.</li> <li><b>Attributes</b>. I was thinking Resistance 9 and Power / Finesse 6 each.</li> <li><b>Influences</b>. Banks 1, Cars 1, Cinemas 1, Commerce 1, Restaurants 1, Stores 1.</li> <li><b>Manifestations</b>. Twilight Form, Discorporate, Reaching, Shadow Gateway</li> <li><b>Numina</b>. It should have exchanged some Numina for a bit more of influence. Emotional Aura, Implant Mission, Rapture are my current candidates for it to keep.</li> <li><b>Ban</b>. Must be in the presence of someone shopping every 24 hours, otherwise it becomes morose and lethargic losing it\u2019s defense.</li> <li><b>Bane</b>. A human that has been voluntarily poor for a year, like a mendicant monk or an ascetic.</li> <li><b>Aspiration</b>. Also lost here, perhaps something related to buy or use the services of the mall daily? In tune with its zero speed. But this could make the pack completely static, no globetrotting for them.</li> <li><b>Size</b>. This thing is humongous, I am following <a href=\"https://wodan.obsidianportal.com/wikis/size\" target=\"_blank\">this table</a>, but not sure... According to that, my idea of the spirit having the same size as the building this thing would have size 100!</li> <li><b>Speed</b>. Zero, it does not move, ever.</li> <li><b>Totem Advantages</b>. Residential Area? Pack Dynamics? Professional Training?</li> <li><b>Pack Merits</b>. I was thinking of Dedicated Locus, Den, Resources, Safe Place, Staff.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> I appreciate any help making spirit and pack viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-08-2022, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-07T20:34:43-08:00","id":1496453,"title":"","content":"A possibly important thing to remember: the Shadow bears less of a direct resemblance to the material world the thicker the Gauntlet is in the area, which means you can afford for this thing to look weirder than a regular shopping mall.<br /> <br /> Spirits' names tend to be descriptive, and here it may be worth determining if this is just the spirit of the building or the spirit of commerce, community, et cetera that's managed to claim dominion over the area of the mall, which may help somewhat with mobility and (assuming this isn't based on an existing real-world place) figuring out what other spirits call it.<br /> <br /> I'd almost suggest a Ban relating to the mall's operating hours \u2014 with 21 Totem points, you're looking at a Rank 3 spirit, which tend to have bans that aren't so easy to trigger.<br /> <br /> Aspiration-wise it's worth remembering that this relates to the <i>goals</i> of the spirit and the pack. Why and how did the pack take its services as a totem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T07:06:04-08:00","id":1496492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496425-shopping-mall-totem?p=1496453#post1496453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A possibly important thing to remember: the Shadow bears less of a direct resemblance to the material world the thicker the Gauntlet is in the area, which means you can afford for this thing to look weirder than a regular shopping mall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer, I will try to touch your points in detail.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496425-shopping-mall-totem?p=1496453#post1496453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits' names tend to be descriptive, and here it may be worth determining if this is just the spirit of the building or the spirit of commerce, community, et cetera that's managed to claim dominion over the area of the mall, which may help somewhat with mobility and (assuming this isn't based on an existing real-world place) figuring out what other spirits call it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The name of the mall itself I think will suffice as it gives it a distinct identity, tied to humans, with all its components and the things that happen inside as small pieces of it (giving it a very nuanced personality and lots of low value Influences), or as the location that contains everything happening. I envision two alternatives:<ul><li>A large (size 100) immobile spirit, that looms over the other shops and spirits, as the leader of a minor court inside itself, he would be both lord and land.</li> <li>A stereotypical shopper like-being so it seems very approachable and has things to talk about, but always in a transactional way.</li> </ul><br /> Both options have influences Banks 1, Cars 1, Cinemas 1, Commerce 1, Restaurants 1, Stores 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496425-shopping-mall-totem?p=1496453#post1496453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd almost suggest a Ban relating to the mall's operating hours \u2014 with 21 Totem points, you're looking at a Rank 3 spirit, which tend to have bans that aren't so easy to trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a great idea, could you put some examples? I am not really good at making Bans and Banes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496425-shopping-mall-totem?p=1496453#post1496453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspiration-wise it's worth remembering that this relates to the <i>goals</i> of the spirit and the pack. Why and how did the pack take its services as a totem?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a generational pack; elder Iron Masters induct new members in the pack as part of a business continuity plan that also aims to influence the affluent areas around. The Pack wants to keep the area nice, safe, clean and prosperous. It certainly gives them clout with the other packs in the city as being the guys that have a perfect territory and having enough resources to aid the tribe itself... I thought about giving it something related to become a Lodge... Or to continuous prosperity... But I am terrible at these things.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I am trying to balance the size 100 (which would give it incredible resilience) with some limiting factor (speed 0, and Ban/Aspirations related to staying in the same place) to avoid having this thing steamroll opponents by acting as a meat-shield for the Pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-08-2022, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T11:12:03-08:00","id":1496516,"title":"","content":"It needn\u2019t be gargantuan, this totem. Maybe it appears as a mascot of the mall\u2019s most prosperous store? This visage changes over time, with stores falling from the spot and others rising to replace it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T23:37:10-08:00","id":1496578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496425-shopping-mall-totem?p=1496492#post1496492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The name of the mall itself I think will suffice as it gives it a distinct identity, tied to humans, with all its components and the things that happen inside as small pieces of it (giving it a very nuanced personality and lots of low value Influences), or as the location that contains everything happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to take a shot in the dark here and suppose the mall is not named in First Tongue, nor is its human-language name descriptive in the ways the Shadow is likely to care about. What is the character of the mall? Is it anything more than a glorified Allholder? How have changes in stock and ownership (or prevention thereof) affected the personality of the mall as reflected by the spirit over time?<br /> <br /> It is important to remember that spirits aren't the Naturae or city-psyches of the Astral realms; mostly a powerful spirit leaves its mark on its surroundings by partaking of the Essence of its lessers and feeding that Essence back to them, not by being gestalts, especially not at Rank 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I envision two alternatives:<ul><li>A large (size 100) immobile spirit, that looms over the other shops and spirits, as the leader of a minor court inside itself, he would be both lord and land.</li> <li>A stereotypical shopper like-being so it seems very approachable and has things to talk about, but always in a transactional way.</li> </ul><br /> Both options have influences Banks 1, Cars 1, Cinemas 1, Commerce 1, Restaurants 1, Stores 1. </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is fine-slicing more than needed for Influences, and also with the Totem point totals described this is a spirit right in the middle of the Rank where spirits start being considered full participants in Shadow politics instead of animals and children like Gafflings are. If it's self-aware enough to join a descant and still be considered &quot;the spirit of the shopping mall&quot; then it ought to be secure enough in its place in the world to not be trying to directly embody everything in its domain instead of commanding tenant structure-spirits and visiting vehicle spirits and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a generational pack; elder Iron Masters induct new members in the pack as part of a business continuity plan that also aims to influence the affluent areas around. The Pack wants to keep the area nice, safe, clean and prosperous. It certainly gives them clout with the other packs in the city as being the guys that have a perfect territory and having enough resources to aid the tribe itself... I thought about giving it something related to become a Lodge... Or to continuous prosperity... But I am terrible at these things. </div> </div> </div>Think of the mall as a creature made of its structural materials and history and place in the world. It almost certainly wants money circulating through it, but depending on how it's been run, its priorities for maintenance and sustenance will be different. Does this thing put out a lure and wait for food to come to it, or does it have subordinates harry its prey into its metaphorical jaws? Is the process of gentrification manifested in its impact on the Shadow of the surrounding area, or has the pack's stewardship bent it away from that kind of unrestrained predation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally, I am trying to balance the size 100 (which would give it incredible resilience) with some limiting factor (speed 0, and Ban/Aspirations related to staying in the same place) to avoid having this thing steamroll opponents by acting as a meat-shield for the Pack. </div> </div> </div>I will repeat: if this is the spirit of one of the oldest buildings of its type in the area and has functional sovereignty within its domain, it is probably above the pay grade of a mid-Rank 3 pack totem, whose fortunes are very strongly tied up in the pack's continued loyalty and survival.<br /> <br /> Have you considered approaching this concept as a lodge or protectorate first, with the mall being the hub/connective tissue between different packs' efforts to steer the development of the city around it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T09:23:37-08:00","id":1496600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496425-shopping-mall-totem?p=1496578#post1496578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to take a shot in the dark here and suppose the mall is not named in First Tongue, nor is its human-language name descriptive in the ways the Shadow is likely to care about. What is the character of the mall? Is it anything more than a glorified Allholder? How have changes in stock and ownership (or prevention thereof) affected the personality of the mall as reflected by the spirit over time?<br /> <br /> It is important to remember that spirits aren't the Naturae or city-psyches of the Astral realms; mostly a powerful spirit leaves its mark on its surroundings by partaking of the Essence of its lessers and feeding that Essence back to them, not by being gestalts, especially not at Rank 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>First thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> I would like to point that this spirit is artificially relevant, the only reason it is important is due to the constant effort of the Pack to make it more important than it is. And yes the mall name in English would be its name, so if the place is called Palisades, that would be its name.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496425-shopping-mall-totem?p=1496578#post1496578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this is fine-slicing more than needed for Influences, and also with the Totem point totals described this is a spirit right in the middle of the Rank where spirits start being considered full participants in Shadow politics instead of animals and children like Gafflings are. If it's self-aware enough to join a descant and still be considered &quot;the spirit of the shopping mall&quot; then it ought to be secure enough in its place in the world to not be trying to directly embody everything in its domain instead of commanding tenant structure-spirits and visiting vehicle spirits and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got you, but as per my previous comment in this post, the spirit itself depends a lot on the pack, it has outsourced to say it in another way, most of its relevance to the pack, so it punches above his weight class due to the Uratha tending to it. Uratha that make their best to make the spirit pliant and subservient; the totem is a valuable part of the pack, but the pack are not servants to this spirit, a pack member would put it <i>&quot;We are not Pure, in the pecking order we are above most spirits here, Palisades included&quot;. </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496425-shopping-mall-totem?p=1496578#post1496578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of the mall as a creature made of its structural materials and history and place in the world. It almost certainly wants money circulating through it, but depending on how it's been run, its priorities for maintenance and sustenance will be different. Does this thing put out a lure and wait for food to come to it, or does it have subordinates harry its prey into its metaphorical jaws? Is the process of gentrification manifested in its impact on the Shadow of the surrounding area, or has the pack's stewardship bent it away from that kind of unrestrained predation?</div> </div> </div> </div>The pack has carefully cultivated the influences of the spirit, they want it to embody all the region qualities they like, but not too much of anything. <i>&quot;We want you to be important but not important enough to overshadow us&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496425-shopping-mall-totem?p=1496578#post1496578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will repeat: if this is the spirit of one of the oldest buildings of its type in the area and has functional sovereignty within its domain, it is probably above the pay grade of a mid-Rank 3 pack totem, whose fortunes are very strongly tied up in the pack's continued loyalty and survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the idea, that this spirit be dependent on the Pack's loyalty and survival.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496425-shopping-mall-totem?p=1496578#post1496578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you considered approaching this concept as a lodge or protectorate first, with the mall being the hub/connective tissue between different packs' efforts to steer the development of the city around it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it was part of my options, but I am just not good at this part.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a very, <i>very </i>rough stat setting that I have for the spirit so far:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Totem:</b> Palisades<br /> <br /> <b>Totem Type:</b> Multiplex Spirit<br /> <b>Description</b>: Palisades is identical to his material counterpart.<br /> <b>Aspirations</b>: The mall must grow.<br /> <b>Totem Points</b>: 21<br /> <b>Rank</b>: 3<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Power 6, Finesse 6, Resistance 9<br /> <b>Willpower</b>: 10<br /> <b>Essence</b>: 20<br /> <b>Initiative</b>: 15<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 6<br /> <b>Speed</b>: 0<br /> <b>Size</b>: 100<br /> <b>Corpus</b>: 109<br /> <b>Influences</b>: Banks 1, Cars 1, Cinema 1, Commerce 1, Restaurants 1, Stores 1<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Twilight Form, Discorporate, Reaching, Shadow Gateway<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Emotional Aura, Implant Mission, Rapture; 3 Numina exchanged for Influence dots<br /> <b>Ban</b>: Palisades must be in the presence of someone shopping every 24 hours, otherwise it becomes morose and lethargic losing it\u2019s defense.<br /> <b>Bane</b>: A human that has been voluntarily poor for a year, like a mendicant monk or an ascetic.<br /> <b>Totem Advantage</b>: Merit: Residential Area 5, Merit: Pack Dynamics 5<br /> <b>Pack Merits</b>: Dedicated Locus 5, Den 5, Resources 5, Safe Place 5, Staff 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T16:18:01-08:00","id":1496658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496425-shopping-mall-totem?p=1496600#post1496600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to point that this spirit is artificially relevant, the only reason it is important is due to the constant effort of the Pack to make it more important than it is. And yes the mall name in English would be its name, so if the place is called Palisades, that would be its name.<br /> <br /> Got you, but as per my previous comment in this post, the spirit itself depends a lot on the pack, it has outsourced to say it in another way, most of its relevance to the pack, so it punches above his weight class due to the Uratha tending to it. Uratha that make their best to make the spirit pliant and subservient; the totem is a valuable part of the pack, but the pack are not servants to this spirit, a pack member would put it <i>&quot;We are not Pure, in the pecking order we are above most spirits here, Palisades included&quot;. </i><br /> <br /> The pack has carefully cultivated the influences of the spirit, they want it to embody all the region qualities they like, but not too much of anything. <i>&quot;We want you to be important but not important enough to overshadow us&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> That is the idea, that this spirit be dependent on the Pack's loyalty and survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The totem's name should be a short epithet, reflecting [the totem's character] concept.&quot; People who know about it might refer to it by the name of the mall, but an epithet is a descriptive phrase, not a borrowed location-name.<br /> <br /> I'm going to just reiterate here that what you are describing is <i>a territory the pack has under their control</i>, not an individual totem spirit strong enough to be a major participant in local politics. You don't get Rank 3 spirits who aren't important \u2014 Rank <i>is </i>importance in the Shadow's hierarchy and ecosystem, and if a werewolf is above a Rank 3 spirit that werewolf is the stuff of legends.<br /> <br /> Either the spirit is actually important or it's serving as the political mascot for a pack with a lot of collective pull separate from that provided by its spiritual representative. The Shadow deals in metaphor by consequence in the medium of hungry creatures made of symbolism, not pure conceptual manifestations where &quot;the spirit of the mall&quot; has to mean &quot;the mall itself, which we're giving magic powers and calling a spirit.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}